Add support for OpenGL ES

This compilation error occurs because GL_UNSIGNED_INT_8_8_8_8_REV is part of
full desktop OpenGL (1.2+), but we are building with headers configured for
OpenGL ES (GLES) or missing the desktop OpenGL extension headers.

In texture initialization (glTexImage2D or glTexSubImage2D), substituting
GL_UNSIGNED_INT_8_8_8_8_REV with GL_UNSIGNED_BYTE matches standard 8-bit per
channel RGBA/BGRA buffers across both GLES and desktop OpenGL.

